    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does LinkedIn lead generation work for a Pune manufacturing SME?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">LinkedIn lead generation for B2B Manufacturing, Industrial + Engineering Exports in Pune combines 4 mechanisms: (1) LinkedIn Sales Navigator search + list building (target procurement heads + tender committees + international buyers + industry-specific OEMs), (2) Personalised connection + InMail sequences (proven templates + industry-native writing), (3) LinkedIn Ads (Sponsored Content + Message Ads + Conversation Ads + Lead Gen Forms), (4) Retargeting + CRM integration + weekly qualified-lead delivery to your team. Buyer intent: RFQ + tender inclusion + capability-deck-download. Pune buyer educated + culturally-Maharashtrian + values authenticity + long-cycle relationship. LinkedIn used for BD + talent + industry-association engagement. Rising founder ecosystem.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is a realistic monthly retainer for LinkedIn lead generation for a Pune manufacturing SME?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">In Pune: Rs 60,000-1.5 lakh Starter (Sales Nav + connection + InMail + basic Ads), Rs 1.5-3 lakh Growth (full-stack outbound + Ads + retargeting + CRM integration + weekly qualified-lead delivery), Rs 3-6 lakh Enterprise (multi-persona + multi-territory + inside-sales support + advanced attribution). Ad spend separate: Rs 40K-4 lakh/month depending on tier + CPL benchmark. Rs 400-2,000 CPQL for qualified procurement lead.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does LinkedIn Sales Navigator work for lead generation?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Sales Navigator is LinkedIn's premium lead-search tool (Rs 5,000-8,000/month per seat). Capabilities: (1) Advanced search — filter by industry + role + seniority + geography + company-size + tech-stack + recent job change + intent signal, (2) Saved searches — get notified when new prospects match your criteria, (3) Lead + account lists — organise prospects for outreach, (4) InMail credits — direct message anyone (not just 1st connections), (5) TeamLink — leverage your team's connections + warm intros. For a Pune manufacturing SME, Sales Navigator is ROI-positive from month 2 onwards. ITD manages Sales Navigator as part of Growth + Enterprise tiers.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is a realistic CPQL (cost per qualified lead) for a Pune manufacturing SME via LinkedIn?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">In Pune: Rs 400-2,000 CPQL for qualified procurement lead. Qualified-lead-to-transaction conversion: 5-15% qualified-lead-to-RFQ conversion, 15-30% RFQ-to-order for well-positioned suppliers. Effective cost per acquired customer varies by industry + AOV — for high-AOV/LTV segments (banking + consulting + real-estate), LinkedIn CPL is typically 2-5x higher than Meta/Google but qualified-lead quality is 3-10x higher + closed-revenue attribution justifies the premium.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What LinkedIn Ads formats work best for lead generation?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Sponsored Content (native feed ads) — text + image or video, best for awareness + engagement. (2) Sponsored InMail / Message Ads — direct message to target audience inbox, 20-40% open rate, best for high-value outreach. (3) Conversation Ads — interactive branching-message ads, 3-5x engagement vs static InMail. (4) Lead Gen Forms — auto-fill from LinkedIn profile, best for high-volume qualified inbound. (5) Document Ads — PDF/carousel delivered in-feed, best for whitepaper + report distribution. For Pune manufacturing SME, best mix: 40-50% Sponsored Content + 25-30% Message Ads + 15-20% Conversation Ads + 10-15% Lead Gen Forms.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we handle personalised connection + InMail sequences for a Pune manufacturing SME?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">ITD's outbound sequence workflow: (1) Sales Navigator targeting — build list of 200-500 target procurement heads + tender committees + international buyers + industry-specific OEMs matching your ICP, (2) Personalised connection request with brief context (no pitch — earn the connection), (3) 3-5 day post-connection engagement — like + comment on their content to build familiarity, (4) First InMail/message with value-first framing (industry insight or specific relevance to their business), (5) 7-14 day follow-up with resource/insight/case study, (6) 30-day nurture with content sharing + relationship building. Response rates in Pune: 15-35% for well-crafted sequences (vs 2-8% for generic templates).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
